  "changelog": "method-grammar-diagnostic v1.0.0 \u2014 First release for diagnosing grammar and syntax issues in psychology methods sections.\n\n- Provides comprehensive analysis and scoring on verb tense, passive/active voice, sentence structure, and precise grammar rules, based directly on Science Research Writing (2nd ed.) \u00a72.5.1 and related checklists.\n- Outputs scores and grades for four diagnostic dimensions with itemized error breakdowns and auto-selects top-journal positive examples for core problems.\n- Delivers actionable revision suggestions following detected issue severity, following a transparent, structured reporting template.\n- Integrates directly with related skills for structure, logic, and vocabulary under the psychology-academic-writing domain.\n- All diagnostic criteria, scoring rubric, and exemplar matches are fully documented and traceable to explicit academic sources.",
